Pick a floating workspace directory from the web client

In the tile, Settings > Floating Workspace > Terminal Directory's folder button
did nothing - no picker, no error - and no directory could be applied. The
desktop feature is three host operations the browser had a path for none of: a
native OS dialog, the trust grant that dialog also performs, and a cwd
resolution that only returns a custom path once it is trusted. The tile's
floating terminals run on the workspace host, so all three must happen there.

Two runtime methods, `floatingWorkspace.resolveCwd` and `grantDirectory`, reuse
the existing `ipc/floating-workspace-directory.ts` helpers, and the web client
opens the existing `RemoteFileBrowser`, then grants and stores what was picked.
Both authorize or mutate host state, so neither is on
`MOBILE_RPC_METHOD_ALLOWLIST`.

The grant is a precondition, not a courtesy: a refused directory is not stored
and the server's own reason is shown. Storing one anyway would resolve to '',
which the input renders as the configured path, so the pane would display a
directory the server never authorised while the floating terminal opened
somewhere else.

Desktop is not left untouched, and the one change is deliberate.
`getFloatingWorkspaceDirectoryInputValue` returns the configured path when the
resolve has not answered yet, where upstream returned the empty resolve. Without
it the field blanks between picking a directory and the round trip returning -
imperceptible over desktop IPC, a visible flicker over a network hop. Desktop
sees the same fallback, and only during that window, because a stored path is
now always one the server accepted.

To test, pick a directory in Settings > Floating Workspace in the tile, confirm
it is displayed back, then open a floating terminal and check its cwd; then pick
one the server cannot grant and confirm the field does not change and the
failure is reported. Covered by `floating-workspace.test.ts`,
`FloatingWorkspacePane.test.tsx`,
`floating-workspace-directory-grant.test.ts` and
`mobile-rpc-allowlist.test.ts`.
